## Contrast: Full v2 Implementation in adb_server_device_commands.rs

The upstream server-device code has the complete shell v2 decoder:

```rust
// adb_server_device_commands.rs:163-266
fn shell_command_v2(
    &self,
    command: &dyn AsRef<str>,
    mut stdout: Option<&mut dyn Write>,
    mut stderr: Option<&mut dyn Write>,
) -> Result<Option<u8>> {
    // ...
    let mut exit = None;
    let mut input = std::io::BufReader::new(self.transport.get_raw_connection()?);

    loop {
        // PARSE 5-byte frame header
        let mut pckt_metadata = vec![0; 5];
        input.read_exact(&mut pckt_metadata)?;

        let channel = pckt_metadata[0];
        let payload_size = u32::from_le_bytes(pckt_metadata[1..5].try_into()?);

        // ROUTE by stream-id
        match ShellChannel::try_from(channel)? {
            ShellChannel::Stdout | ShellChannel::Stderr => {
                // Read payload_size bytes, route to appropriate writer
                // ...read loop...
            }
            ShellChannel::ExitStatus => {
                // VALIDATE exit frame has exactly 1 byte
                if payload_size != 1 {
                    return Err(RustADBError::ADBShellV2ParseError(
                        format!("Spurious exit status packet with size of {payload_size} (should be 1)")
                    ));
                }
                // READ 1 byte as exit code
                exit = Some(input.read_u8()?);
            }
        }
    }
    Ok(exit)  // <-- Returns captured exit code
}
```

This is a **working reference**. persistent.rs has none of it.

